My 1st ascension was not too long ago. This is my second but not
sequential.I killed a monk who decided to eat a cockatrice after
getting to AC:-1 naked. Quite a shame. Then I killed a couple
of cavemen before I started this game.

It seems to me that the most important thing to do is to
appropriately name my characters. If I think long and hard about
a name for that class, I usually play better. My 1st ascension
was a chaotic female wizard named Morgan Le Fay. For this I
decided to pick a chaotic healer named after the TV show
character House. I played around too much in the end and
decided it would be better to ascend than run out of "oLS and
die for good.

House started his quest as a quasi-pacifist. That is he killed
things but carefully watched his XP and made sure he didn't XP2.
There was a lawful altar on level one and a neutral one on level
two with the branch to the mines. House gathered (stole) as much
money as he could and with the help of his pet cat conned some
shopkeeps out of their gold. He managed to buy down to naked
AC 0 in minetown and went back to the main dungeon to look for
more gold and play sokoban. Being a smart chap, sokoban was no
trouble. With enough food and a "oR he went back to the alter
and sacfested for a bit. Was gifted the magicbane which seemed
odd. I thought he was supposed to get something else first.

He then started looking for a bag of holding as his stash on
Dlvl 2 was getting too large. He found a cloak of MR in a shop
along with some water walking boots. By now he had bought enough
to have naked AC: -2. He had a crystal plate mail and had found
an unidentified helmet with no negative effects. With this his
AC was somewhere in the mid negative teens somewhere. He of
course also had a cheap pair of gloves. With this and his cat
and a new puppy he went to the bottom of the mines and got luck
and touch stones.

A poly trap gave him a pet Nalfeshnee and Jabberwock with the
help of a magic whistle. He found a magic lamp on his way down
and wished himself the Eye of the Aethiopica. He seemed to
remember being a wizard who died in many previous lives. These
two pets helped him kill all the shopkeepers but he kept the
chaotic priest at minetown alive for fun.

So house explored the main dungeon. Still no bag of holding and
with this crystal platemail the stash got large quickly cause
he found it hard to keep himself unencumbered. At level 10 a
huge surprise, a double bones file. House had a dejavu moment
from another life when he saw a master Lich at the bottom of
the stairs. A Wizard and Monk had both been killed by him.

House tried his best to kill the master lich, but so many big
nasties got summoned, he would only get 1 turn at a time at the
stairs bottom. So he explored the previous parts of the dungeon
some more eventually getting up to about XP 15 and 170 HP. This
gave him 2 turns at the bottom of the stairs.Unfortunately the
nalfeshnee got killed by the big nasties but the jabberwock
survived (by not attacking anything!!). Then while healing
himself at the top of the stairs house saw his opportunity as a
cockatrice walked into the room.

Quickly he used a wand of MM to kill it and was ecstatic that
it left a corpse.Picking it up he noticed he was burdened. This
meant he had to use one turn to wield the corpse every time at
the stairs bottom. Eventually he had a nice collection of
statues. House revived some nasties one at a time and killed
them properly, except the lich who he shattered with a pickaxe
and made meatballs.

A wave of psychic energy poured over House. One big nasty left.
Unfortunately no cockatrice corpse left. Carefully house put
some grease on his helmut and readied himself for battle with
what he feared the most (brainlessness). When house flung a bolt
 of MM at the master mindflayer he got an unpleasant surprise.
The mindflayer had picked "oR, cloak of MR, a wand of digging
and likely several scrolls of teleportation off the bones file.
Luckily House had a unicorn horn for the many times that bastard
ate his brains. In the end he never found where this mindflayer
ended up. He avoided genociding them for a long time looking.

The bones files were helpful. 2 bags of holding both cursed.
Without cancellation, house could not uncurse the bags because
they were too heavy to dip in holy water. Upon looting one he
noticed a magic lamp, or at least what he thought might have
been one. He tried to get it out on the first attempt but had
already selected too many items to fit in his pack.
House decided to leave that bag alone till he could find a wand
of cancellation. The other bag had no lamp in it, House took
out as many useful items as possible destroying many in the
process, but now he had a BoH. The Jabberwock got really
friendly with the chaotic priest at the alter on this level and
gave house a robe. House also took a cursed Sunsword,
Snickersnee, Sting and Fire Brand on these piles.

Though he would have sworn he should have taken that left turn
in Albuquerque, House eventually found his way up to some store
of goods that looked oddly familiar. In it he found some
blessed clear potions and decided to test their affect on a
cursed BoH.

He also decided he needed to ID some more things but had no
other way than the dangerous one. He carefully quaffed potions
and read scrolls wearing sacrificial armor. Bad things happened
to him. He played with an iron ball for a little while before
praying on his altar to get it unattached. He found a wand of
create monster and took a break to sacfest. Eventually he
thought he was ready and continued. His god gifted him a
spellbook of ID eventually along with MM. Making his
experiments unnecessary with the robe in his BoH.

At XP 19 House decided to try the quest. How hard can this
Cyclops be anyway? On his way in he killed a silver dragon
and found an amulet of lifesaving. He decided to use an enchant
armor and stash the "oR. This also meant he could ditch the
heavy crystal plate mail. With AC well below -20 now House was
confident, he was going to kick the cyclop's ass. His
Snickersnee was +5 as his alternate weapon to magicbane and he
was at least Basic in both (probably better). Unfortunately,
Cyclops drained levels like a madman. House ran back upstairs
and was followed my the Cyclops! Down to less than 50HP and
level 5 it was time for desperate measures. Apply the Eye and
portal out leaving the pet jabberwock behind. After being
blasted he had 10HP... that was close.

House slowly worked his XP and confidence back up. Eventually,
he found a ring of polymorph control to complement his ring of
polymorph. He went back to his stash and polyied into a Xorn
for some yummy rings. This gave him a modest too hit and damage
bonus. He also noticed that he felt like a new woman. With
Charisma about 10 she was not a very pretty woman either. But
this affords a new opportunity. After waiting a bit House put
the rings back on and presto-chango became a silver dragon.
Placing a few eggs in her pack, she smiled as she thought of
one day riding on top of them to demigoddessness.

One hatched and she named it Deathmonger. She took deathmonger
around hoping to find a saddle, but instead found a very curious
thing in the mines. A black pudding slimmed its way next to her.
Her scientific mind made her prod it with a key. And with this
the pudding became 2 with half the health. She continued to
experiment with puddings while Deathmonger became stronger.
She also got another "oLS (where the 1st came from I'm not sure)
and a /cancellation.

After totally boring her real world counterpart nearly to death.
The pudding farming ended. She remembered that lamp she so
wanted and thought to herself of what she would wish for.
Stupidly, she wished for the only other thing she new would give
leveldrain resistance: Stormbringer. With a very low likelihood
of success (probably 0% with wrong alignment) it slipped threw
her fingers. So that was one wasted wish. She explored nearly
all of the main dungeon with her friendly pet Deathmonger
giving him as many meatballs as she could muster and making
sure he stayed healthy with a stethoscope. She stormed the
castle and claimed her wand of wishing (0:1). Having wasted her
scrolls of charging on rings, she decided to polypile some
stuff with a wand of polymorph she had stashed.

Stupidest mistake of game:

She inadvertently dropped her wand of wishing on the pile and
lost it :-(

My next ascension may be wishless. I seem to do okay with all
the wishes I waste.


Her polypiling had also yielded a saddle for Deathmonger. She
found a pair of speedboots from the armory. Her old helmut was
a helm of brilliance and once enchanted with an old pair of
gauntlets of dexterity and robe her spellcasting was awesome.
Anyway she got enough scrolls of enchant armor to get her AC
below -40 all fixed. Another thing she got was a +5 ring of
adornment and plenty of gain ability potions. Now she could
chat with and incubus any time she felt like it. Her reflection
in a mirror was also quite breathtaking "you look a beautiful
as ever".

Time to try old one-eye again. This time things went well, She
slashed him right in the face with her now +7 Snickersnee while
Deathmonger also attacked. She only came out at XP level 19 and
burned one amulet of life saving. She then used some BUC scrolls
of enchant weapon to get +7 Staff of Aesculapius.Incidentally
this was my first time playing the healer quest.

Now she felt ready for some Wraiths since she had already
gotten some practice off a cheap staff earlier. Riding
Deathmonger into the valley of the dead she used the Eye to make
a portal to Sokoban to try to take them outside the graveyard.
On the way down again she found Fort Ludious. And got about
$100000.She gave all this money in 400*XP to the priest in the
valley. This gave her naked AC: -5 Her lowest in the game.

She played around for a long time until she was XP30+ before
entering Gehennom. At some point she was having fun sacrificing
stuff on an altar and made a very rash move of sacrificing her
own race. This angered Hermes so much she went from naked AC -5
to 10. She did gain a bit back but continued to try to anger
various gods and lost any protection right back.

On her first trip into Gehennom she somehow lost Deathmonger
while not riding him. This was disappointing, there was a backup
saddle in the castle but her good friend, it seemed, was gone.
Amazingly, thousands of turns later, she found Deathmonger and
he was still tame. She pressed on into Vlad's tower where she
found her first wand of death. Unfortunately, she didn't even
ID it before a blast of lightning disintegrated it. I'm not
sure how this happened with reflection, maybe she was
enchanting armor or something and had her SDSM off. But that
seems quite unlikely. One mistake she made on the way down was
her magic whistle was assigned a Z and the bell of opening a z.
So she used all the charges in the bell quite accidentally. She
used another wish from a magic lamp on a wand of polymorph so
she could polypile some scrolls.

She managed to find 2 more wands of death in the entire game.
Orcus used all his charges so she had to charge that one. The
way down went relatively smooth for House. She marked the
vibrating square lit and dug quick routes for the ascent
whenever possible. She returned to her stash and organized
everything, allowing deathmonger to kill the priest with
$165000. She left this and all her gems in a blessed BoH named
LOOT right next to the Dlvl 1upstair.

On her way back down she accidentally let Deathmonger eat a
chameleon corpse while riding him. He became a stupid elf lord.
She then decided nothing but a silver dragon would do (Recalling
how Morgan Le Fay got her saddle disintegrated riding a red
dragon). So she used polymorph control and along the way felt
like a new man. This wreaked his chances of laying silver
dragon eggs. So he continued to polymorph requesting human each
time until he became a woman. This wreaked the player stats
especially constitution, but she did not care.

Waiting a little while, she polyied into a silver dragon and
laid two eggs. Unfortunately she realized she had forgotten to
take off her +5 blessed fireproof Hawaiian shirt. She burned
her last wish for a blessed fireproof +3 T-Shirt. Taking the
young dragons on a tour of the dungeon she named the first one
to reach adulthood RodneyMonger. Saddled him up and went for
the bottom. Deathmonger and the other silver dragon died rather
quickly, but RodneyMonger lived up to her name and helped all
the way to the planes.

There were plenty of cockatrices in Moloch's Sanctum. With
conflict and a +5 small shield she had picked up, She made a
nice collection of statues. Being scientifically minded and a
bit sadistic, she experimented with the stoning process of the
high priest of Moloch. This very much angered Moloch until she
got the message that he was impressed that I survived his death
blasts.

So after claiming the amulet she began her climb atop
RodneyMonger. She continued to fling death rays at Rodney
whenever he appeared often taking advantage of placing her steed
next to him to bounce the ray back. Sometimes she just used a
wall for this purpose. Yeenoghu was summoned somehow on the way
up. He was quite annoying and House decided to teach him a
lesson by showing him how the stoning process works repeatedly.

On Dlvl 1. She realized the bag of LOOT still made her stressed
even with gauntlets of power. So she ended up removing about
$65000 to make herself only burdened. She climbed the stairs
with RodneyMonger and killed Rodney for the last time. She had a
typo and lost RodneyMonger on the plane of earth by stepping
into the portal too soon.

The plane of air was interesting. She looked in her bag of
holding and couldn't find her levitation boots. Apparently the
were in her purse somewhere, but she didn't notice they were in
her main inventory. She plodded her way along to the portal
using confused scrolls of taming to get quite and entourage and
conflict.

Conflict helped her slip by the annoying fire plane. She still
had not noticed her levitation boots in her main inventory so
it was quite traumatic. The plane of water was not so bad
conflict and MM did the job well. She didn't have the sense to
take off her ring of conflict before entering the portal.

Once on the astral plane House became very greedy and a
murderer. She decided she wanted to tame two of the riders. So
she went first to pestilence wearing her stunning amulet of life
saving holding the staff and a unicorn horn handy.She dropped
her bag of LOOT on the altar so she was unencumbered. Pestilence
became a pansy quite quickly against the staff. She was now able
to give one hit deaths too him. The sickness was annoying but
not so bad with the staff and a unicorn horn. However she soon
noticed that her unicorn horn became cursed, already on her
backup from before. Why do malignant aura's always seem to go
for unicorn horns? So confused, hallucinating, stunned blind
and ill she was ignored by the staff. She burned an amulet of
lifesaving and quickly put another one on. She then read a
taming scroll, I'm not sure how being blinded. After this she
noticed she had burned another amulet of lifesaving. Oh crap she
thought she may run out of amulets. So she stumbled over to the
altar and found her bag of LOOT missing :-( Oh well, better to
ascend than to die. Hey that's where my levitation boots are
she exclaimed as the choir began to sing. In total she died 3
times against Pestilence. Did she succeed in taming
Pestilence? The world will never know.


